cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use or reference this work, please cite it as below."
title: "Blitz-Swarm: Config-driven parallel multi-agent research swarm on local CLIs"
type: software
authors:
  - given-names: Joona
    family-names: Tyrninoksa
repository-code: "https://github.com/Joona-t/blitz-swarm"
license: MIT
version: "0.3.0"
date-released: "2026-10-11"
abstract: >-
  A parallel multi-agent research swarm that runs every agent as a subprocess
  of a local CLI (Claude Code, Codex, Gemini, Ollama, any OpenAI-compatible
  server or any argv-templated CLI) with no paid token API on a default path.
  Consensus mode stages round 1 (researchers, then evaluators, then a judge
  ensemble), blasts later rounds in parallel through a shared blackboard that
  is read back for every context, stops on evaluator unanimity with a holdout
  override, and preserves unresolved dissent. Mythos mode runs a deep planner,
  parallel executors and a deep verifier (Fable 5.1 on the Claude CLI by
  default) with a subprocess test gate. Models are resolved from configuration
  through one role-to-tier-to-model function; a three-tier G-Memory store
  (SQLite FTS5, optional vectors) persists and retrieves across runs. 745
  tests pass without invoking a model. No live benchmark run has been
  executed; the limitations are documented.
keywords:
  - multi-agent systems
  - parallel execution
  - consensus mechanisms
  - dissent preservation
  - G-Memory
  - local LLM CLIs
